{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And if an altar of stones.</b> Rashi explained: every 'if' in the Torah is optional, except for three, etc. And one should not raise a difficulty from 'and if a ransom is imposed on him' — that is only according to what eventuates, when the matter comes about. 'And if <b>an altar of stones</b>' — even if you wish to make Me an altar, you shall build it of whole stones, for this reason. <b>You shall not build them of hewn stone</b> — for stonemasons are accustomed to make engravings on hewn stones, and even without iron, for a chipped stone is invalid in any case, as it is written, 'whole stones you shall build.' 'For your sword' — if <b>you have waved your sword over it and defiled it</b> — by mere touching, for an unspecified sword is of iron, and iron invalidates by touching, as it is written, 'you shall not wave iron over them'; thus our Sages taught in tractate Middot." "<b>And defiled it.</b> We have heard the punishment — the admonition we have not heard. Therefore it says, 'you shall not wave iron over them.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:09.546979879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}